#
# Files listed here are exempted from `guardian audit` scanning.
# Each line is one path relative to the project root, followed by
# a required reason after a `#` character. Lines without a reason
# are rejected. Empty lines and pure-comment lines are ignored.
#
# This file is the centralized, reviewable alternative to the
# per-file `otlc-guardian:audit-exempt` marker. The marker is fine
# for end-user projects where adding a header comment is the
# easiest path. The Guardian repo itself uses this file because:
#
#   1. Every addition is a single visible diff line in PR review.
#   2. The reason field forces the contributor to justify the
#      exemption — no silent additions sneaking past review.
#   3. CI counts the lines and fails if the count grows without
#      a matching CHANGELOG.md entry (see .github/workflows).
#   4. CODEOWNERS can require security-team review of any change
#      to this file.
#
# Format:
#   <relative-path>  # reason: <one-line justification>
#
# ============================================================

